  "synthesis": "All 21 items are published articles, mostly computational pipelines combining public transcriptomic datasets with network pharmacology, WGCNA, machine learning, Mendelian randomization, scRNA-seq, docking, or MD simulation. Metabolic and organelle-stress themes recur: succinylation-related signatures in Alzheimer's disease (NDUFA1, NDUFS5), mitophagy-related hub genes in focal segmental glomerulosclerosis and atherosclerosis, ferroptosis linked to PLCB3 in HFpEF, and multi-omics subtyping of polycystic metabolic ovarian syndrome. Validation is often limited; BATF, for example, was not validated against adjudicated VTE events. The 3.4 rise ratio reflects published counts only. The items do not establish reasons for the increase, and no preprints, code, or industry signals accompany it.",
